            <ArticleTitle>[Directions of investigations for new drugs in asthma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bronchial asthma is affecting more than 300 million people worldwide and in every 15-20 years additional 100 million patients are expected. About 5-10% of asthmatic patients have severe disease and fails to respond to conventional therapy. For this reason a new therapy or improvement in available treatment are under investigations. More knowledge of asthma mechanisms has led to monoclonal antibody, inhaled anti-oxidants and new combination therapy with corticosteroids. Similarly, biological agents directed against IL-13 and immunomodulators influenced T-regulatory cells are likely to be successful in the future therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
